BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Media School
DTSTART:20261120T150000Z
DTEND:20261120T173000Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Happiness 2.0 mask workshop
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the fall semester\, Indiana University undergradua
 te and high school students from the Bloomington community are invited to
  participate in the Happiness 2.0 Mask Workshops — an interactive exper
 ience that brings together science\, art\, and reflection on digital life
 .  The experience combines three components:an accessible discussion of c
 urrent research on digital media and identity  a guided exploration of ar
 tworks in the Eskenazi Museum's galleries  a hands-on mask-making activit
 y    Drawing inspiration from both the research discussion and the museum
  experience\, participants will create a mask representing aspects of the
 ir own digital identity and experiences with digital media. Topics explor
 ed throughout the workshop include identity formation\, online self-prese
 ntation\, the relationship between online and offline selves\, and well-b
 eing.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  Throughout the f
 all semester\, Indiana University undergraduate and high school students 
 from the Bloomington community are invited to participate in the Happines
 s 2.0 Mask Workshops — an interactive experience that brings together s
 cience\, art\, and reflection on digital life.</p><p>  The experience com
 bines three components:</p><ul><li>an accessible discussion of current re
 search on digital media and identity  </li><li>a guided exploration of ar
 tworks in the Eskenazi Museum's galleries  </li><li>a hands-on mask-makin
 g activity  </li></ul><p>  Drawing inspiration from both the research dis
 cussion and the museum experience\, participants will create a mask repre
 senting aspects of their own digital identity and experiences with digita
 l media. Topics explored throughout the workshop include identity formati
 on\, online self-presentation\, the relationship between online and offli
 ne selves\, and well-being.</p>
UID:20261120T150000Z-2396831@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260826T110343Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/mediaiub/event/2396831-happiness-20-mask-workshop
